---
import '@fontsource/yuji-syuku';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Yoruyaki - October 2026';

---

<BaseLayout title={title} />
<main>
  <span class='date'>2026.10.24</span>
  <section>
    <h2>コース</h2>
    <div class='items'>
      <p>A set course to open the meal with edamame, pickles, potato salad, soup, six skewers and rice. After being served feel free to order any other skewers you see below or on the hanging board.</p>
      <div class='item'>
        <h3>枝豆</h3>
        <p>boiled young soybeans, salt</p>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <h3>ぬか漬け</h3>
        <p>assorted rice bran pickles</p>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <h3>ポテトサラダ</h3>
        <p>potato, carrot, onion, cucumber, corn, mayo</p>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <h3>スープ</h3>
        <p>chicken broth, dashi, daikon</p>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/sasami'>
          <h3>ささみ</h3>
          <p>tender, sake, salt, wasabi</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/nasu'>
          <h3>なす</h3>
          <p>eggplant, tare, ginger</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/mune'>
          <h3>胸</h3>
          <p>breast, yuzu kosho</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/shishitou'>
          <h3>しし唐</h3>
          <p>shishitou pepper, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/negima'>
          <h3>ねぎま</h3>
          <p>thigh, scallion, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/tsukune'>
          <h3>つくね</h3>
          <p>meatball, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <h3>炊き込みご飯</h3>
        <p>rice, chanterelle, lobster mushroom</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>串焼き</h2>
    <div class='items'>
      <p>
        Various types of skewers with limited amounts, click on the name to go to a page with more detail. When ordering check the board to see if they are still available. Shichimi, yuzu kosho, and lemon are available as toppings.
      </p>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/eringi'>
          <h3>エリンギ</h3>
          <p>king oyster mushroom, miso dengaku</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <h3>しいたけ</h3>
        <p>shitake mushroom, tare</p>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/tebamotoreggu'>
          <h3>手羽元レッグ</h3>
          <p>drumette, leg, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/tebanaka'>
          <h3>手羽中</h3>
          <p>wing, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/obisori'>
          <h3>おびそり</h3>
          <p>inner thigh, oyster, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/furisode'>
          <h3>ふりそで</h3>
          <p>shoulder, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/harami'>
          <h3>ハラミ</h3>
          <p>belly, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/kawa'>
          <h3>皮</h3>
          <p>skin, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/bonjiri'>
          <h3>ぼんじり</h3>
          <p>tail, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/seseri'>
          <h3>せせり</h3>
          <p>neck, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/hizanankotsu'>
          <h3>膝軟骨</h3>
          <p>knee cartilage, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/yagennankotsu'>
          <h3>ヤゲン軟骨</h3>
          <p>keel cartilage, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/sunagimo'>
          <h3>砂肝</h3>
          <p>gizzard, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/hatsu'>
          <h3>ハツ</h3>
          <p>heart, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/reba'>
          <h3>レバー</h3>
          <p>liver, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="notes">
    <h2>Notes</h2>
    <p>
      We had 12 guests this time and made 204 skewers with no leftovers. The chicken skewers were pretty much the same as usual, however we did have zucchini skewers that were off menu to test. We just grilled them and then did a dip in tare, but that was lacking a little salt so it would probably be better to do a sake spray and salt before grilling. We'll do these in summer for sure and may continue to do them in winter as well.
    </p>
    <p>
      The main change we've been making is moving back towards more of a course rather than a set to start. We still have the edamame, pickles and potato salad, but dropped the udon this time in favor of doing soup and rice. The soup was stock from the chicken bones, simmer with daikon and finished with konbu and katsuobushi. We then strained and cooked some cubed pieces of daikon in the soup, then removed and placed in bowls ahead of time. As guests arrived we just added hot soup to the bowl. Tram had foraged some chanterelle and lobster mushrooms which is what we used in the mixed rice (takikomigohan). It was delicious!
    </p>
    <p>
      When guests first arrived they received the soup, edamame, pickles, potato salad and two skewers. Once everyone had arrived we took the guests thru four more skewers with everyone getting the same. We then offered takikomigohan to anyone who wanted it. After everyone had been served the same thing we opened up ordering for the rest of the menu. Guest could order two skewers at a time and once they had received those two skewers they could order another two. This gives everyone a chance to try some of the more limited skewers.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

<style>
  main {
    margin: 0 auto;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 75ch;
  }
  .date {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    text-align: right;
  }
  section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 8fr;
  }
  .items {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    column-gap: 1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid rgb(173, 165, 159);
    padding-left: 2.2rem;
  }
  section h2 {
    font-family: 'Yuji Syuku', serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    writing-mode: vertical-lr;
  }
  section h3 {
    font-family: 'Yuji Syuku', serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  section a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .items > p {
    font-style: italic;
    grid-column-start: span 2;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .images {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-items: center;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .images img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 600px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .images iframe {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 600px;
    aspect-ratio: 9 / 16;
    border: none;
  }

  .notes {
    display: block;
  }

  .notes h2 {
    font-family: 'Noto Sans Variable', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: 2rem;
    writing-mode: horizontal-tb;
  }

  .notes a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .notes p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .items {
      padding-left: 1rem;
    }
    p {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>

